# Chapter 9: any AWS call as a step
#
# Besides the kinds that know a service (sqs, dynamodb, eventbridge, lambda, scheduler), `### aws <service>.<Operation>` calls
# any operation of the services on the classpath: the body is the request JSON, `$` the response. In a local environment it
# just runs; against a remote one every mutating call needs a confirmation (that is M4).
# In the IDE: inside a body, Ctrl+Space completes the request's member names from the AWS model (required ones bold) and values
# from what exists (topics, queues, tables ...); in `# @assert $.` it completes paths of the step's last real response; tool
# window → AWS shows everything that exists, double-click writes a read step for it into explore/explore-<env>.scn and runs it.
# @env local
# @var topic = tour-{{uuid}}

### op aws.discover what-exists
# What exists in the environment: the names completion and the AWS tab use.
# @assert $.resources.dynamodb[0].name == estate-messages
{}

### op aws.describe what-publish-takes
# The request shape of SNS Publish from the bundled model: what body completion offers.
# @assert $.input.required[0] == Message
{"service": "sns", "op": "Publish"}

### aws ssm.GetParameter table-name
# @assert $.Parameter.Value == estate-messages
{"Name": "/estate/common/table-name"}

### aws sns.CreateTopic create-topic
# @capture arn = $.TopicArn
{"Name": "{{topic}}"}

### aws sns.Publish publish
# @assert $.MessageId matches /^[0-9a-f-]{36}$/
{"TopicArn": "{{arn}}", "Message": "hello from the tour"}

### aws s3.CreateBucket bucket
{"Bucket": "{{topic}}", "CreateBucketConfiguration": {"LocationConstraint": "eu-central-1"}}

### aws s3.GetBucketLocation where
# @assert $.LocationConstraint == eu-central-1
{"Bucket": "{{topic}}"}

### aws s3.DeleteBucket clean-up
{"Bucket": "{{topic}}"}

### aws sns.DeleteTopic clean-up-topic
{"TopicArn": "{{arn}}"}
